The '''Pantorans''' were [[Color|blue]]-skinned [[near-human]]s native to the [[moon]] [[Pantora]]. They were part of the [[Galactic Republic]], during the waning [[Standard year|years]] of that [[Politics|government]].

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|Don't whisper around a Pantoran, boy! Our hearing is exceptional.|[[Cuata]], to [[Luke Skywalker]]|<ref name="SW35">[[Star Wars (2020) 35|''Star Wars'' (2020) 35]]</ref>}}
[[File:Pantoran_Prisoner_SaV.png|thumb|left|200px|A male Pantoran member of [[Black Sun]]]]
Pantorans were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that looked very [[Near-human|similar]] to [[human]]s. They had two [[Limb|legs]], two arms ending in five-fingered hands, a torso and a single head. Pantorans had blue skin<ref name="DB Pantoran" /> that turned indigo when they blushed,<ref name="RitR">''[[Servants of the Empire: Rebel in the Ranks]]''</ref> and yellow eyes.<ref name="CW:SoI" /> However, at least one Pantoran was known to have blue eyes.<ref name="Common Ground" /> They grew [[hair]] on the top of the head, and, in males, on the lower parts of the face. The color of their hair varied from white and purple to blue and black.<ref name="Trespass" />

Some Pantorans also displayed simple golden facial [[tattoo]]s<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> known simply as [[Pantoran tattoos]]<ref name="Path of Deceit">''[[The High Republic: Path of Deceit]]''</ref> as a status symbol<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> or to represent their clan and family. Given to a Pantoran during [[Youngling|childhood]],<ref name="Path of Deceit" /> these tattoos were based on ancient Pantoran texts.<ref name="Visual Encyclopedia" /> The Pantorans had a greater resilience to low temperatures than humans, showing no signs of discomfort or unease in the frigid environment of Orto Plutonia that humans could only survive in by wearing special insulated clothing.<ref name="Trespass" /> [[Kevmo Zink]] suspected that [[Rodian]]s and Pantorans saw light across a different spectrum but was unsure what the exact difference was.<ref name="Path of Deceit" /> Known individuals ranged from 1.65<ref name="DB CI Papa">{{Databank|chi-eekway-papanoida|Chi Eekway Papanoida}}</ref> to 1.77 [[meter]]s in height.<ref name="DB Chair Papa">{{Databank|chairman-papanoida|Chairman Papanoida}}</ref> The [[Chiss]], a more obscure blue-skinned species, were sometimes mistaken for Pantorans. However, unlike the Pantorans, the Chiss had red eyes. On one occasion, the Chiss [[Imperial Navy]] officer [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo]] wore dark glasses to hide his red eyes, and pose as a Pantoran.<ref name="Thrawn">[[Thrawn (novel)|''Thrawn'']]</ref>

==Society and culture==
[[File:RiyolaKeevan-TravelWeekly.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Riyola Keevan served as captain of the ''Halcyon'' during the New Republic era.]]
Most Pantorans adorned their faces with yellow<ref name="Kindred">{{InsiderCite|159|Kindred Spirits}}</ref> or bright gold<ref name="Path of Deceit" /> tattoos that signified their family affiliation.<ref name="Kindred" /> [[Kiza]] had those markings on her arms.<ref name="Shadow of the Sith" /> Those like [[Lassa Rhayme]], who had no loyalties toward a family, bore no markings at all.<ref name="Kindred" /> The Pantoran regime was a [[Politics|democracy]], and its governing body was the [[Pantoran Assembly]].<ref name="Trespass" />

Pantoran architecture was very vertical: whereas other cultures left their rooftops bare, Pantorans would not waste space, building more structures atop others and planting gardens.<ref name="Dark Disciple">''[[Dark Disciple]]''</ref> Their [[City|cities]] were elegant and somber, built amongst dreary [[Swamp|marshy]] tundra that stretched away beneath overcast skies.<ref name="VE" /> Some Pantorans were known to worship an unnamed [[Moon Goddess|moon goddess]].<ref name="CW:SoI" />

==History==
[[File:Camping_Pantoran_FDSS.png|thumb|left|200px|A Force-sensitive Pantoran hides from the Empire in the wilderness.]]
Pantorans hailed from [[Pantora]],<ref name="Trespass" /> the [[moon]] of the ice [[planet]] [[Orto Plutonia]].<ref name="DB Pantora">{{Databank|pantora|Pantora}}</ref>

In the [[Standard decade|decades]] that led to the [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the autocratic [[Galactic Empire|First Galactic Empire]], the Pantorans were members of the [[Galactic Republic]].<ref name="DB Pantora" /> As such, they had full [[Senator|representation]] in the [[Galactic Senate|Republic Senate]] on [[Coruscant]]. During this time, they explored [[Orto Plutonia]] and believed that nothing lived there.<ref name="Trespass" />

During the [[Clone Wars]], a pan-[[The galaxy|galactic]] conflict that pitted the Galactic Republic against the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], the Pantorans remained loyal to the Republic and a security force of clone troopers was established on Orto Plutonia. When the Republic lost all contact with that force, Pantoran dignitaries accompanied the [[Jedi]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Anakin Skywalker]] to investigate the disappearance of the Republic troopers. The investigation led to the discovery of an indigenous and sentient, if primitive, species called the [[Talz]], who desired only to be left alone and in peace. The leader of the Pantoran government, Chairman Chi Cho, refused to consider diplomacy or cede control of the planet to what he deemed trespassing savages and deliberately escalated the situation into war between his people and the Talz, resulting in his own death. Deeming the chairman's actions illegal, the Pantoran Assembly revoked his authority and granted Senator [[Riyo Chuchi]] the authority to negotiate a peaceful settlement between the Pantoran people and the Talz, formally ceding control of Orto Plutonia to the latter.<ref name="Trespass" />

At some point, the [[Trade Federation]] imposed a [[blockade]] on Pantora, with the intention of forcing the moon's inhabitants to join the Confederacy. Although many Pantorans demanded that their new chairman, [[Notluwiski Papanoida|Papanoida]], yield to the Trade Federation, he chose to rely on Senator Riyo Chuchi instead. Eventually, Chuchi was able to force the Trade Federation into lifting the blockade by threatening to reveal that the Federation had [[Kidnapping of the Papanoida daughters|abducted]] the chairman's daughters.<ref name="CW:SoI">{{TCW|Sphere of Influence}}</ref>

When the Republic collapsed and the [[Galactic Empire]] seized control of the galaxy, Pantora was cut off from the rest of the galaxy. Struggling to come to grips with their new predicament, the Pantoran Assembly split into three factions: the Appeasers, the Republicans, and the Expansionists. The first group believed that integrating with the Empire was the only path to security and economic strength, while the traditionalist Republicans believed the Empire stood in stark opposition to the core principles and values of the Pantoran culture. The Expansionists argued that the forging of treaties with the old slaving and spice trading worlds around them would be their salvation. The Expansionists were the smallest in number, and their position was viewed as abhorrent by most Pantorans.<ref name="EV">''[[Endless Vigil]]''</ref>
Building up a small navy of volunteers, the Assembly cautiously expanded; careful to avoid drawing Imperial attention to their work. Rogue members of the Assembly began to hire [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] and make unofficial deals to free up the flow of information technologies and resources. Despite the vast resources available on Orto Plutonia, Senator Chuchi's treaty still stood, protecting the Talz from Pantoran interference. While many on the Assembly wished to respect the Treaty, others sought to educate the Talz in hopes of integrating the two societies and sharing resources.<ref name="EV" />

During the [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] between the [[First Order]] and the [[Resistance]], a Pantoran female named [[Riyola Keevan]] served as [[captain]] of the [[MPO-1400 Purgill-class star cruiser|MPO-1400 ''Purgill''-class star cruiser]] ''[[Halcyon]]'' during the [[luxury liner]]'s 275th anniversary voyage to [[Batuu]].<ref name="Cruiser">[[Star Wars: Galactic Starcruiser|''Star Wars'': Galactic Starcruiser]]</ref>

